# Prework Foundations

This directory contains the Prework Foundations track for the 60DaysToCloud program. Each week has its own set of steps to follow; with topics, free resources and notes to follow. Also some mini projects that you can build.

Structure:
- Week1_Cloud_Foundations
- Week2_Linux_Networking
- Week3_Infrastructure_as_Code
- Week4_Containers_Kubernetes
- Week5_CICD_Pipelines
- Week6_Cloud_Security
- Week7_Monitoring_AIOps
- Week8_Final_Project

How to use:
- Each week contains a README with goals, suggested contents, and pointers to labs, examples, and templates..
- Use examples/ and templates/ for reusable code and configuration.
- Contribute new content by opening a pull request against the chore/add-weekly-folders branch (or main if you prefer).



Goal

Before diving into cloud services, build a strong base around Linux, Git, Networking, and Cloud models.
These will make every upcoming week easier and more meaningful.

Topics to Learn
	•	Linux: file system, permissions, common commands, services, and logs.
	•	Git & GitHub: commits, branches, pull requests, and merge workflows.
	•	Networking: IP, DNS, ports, routing, and firewalls.
	•	SDLC: how code moves from development → testing → deployment.
	•	Cloud Models: IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS and usage-based billing.

Practice Resources

Linux:
https://kodekloud.com/courses/linux-basics/
https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Git & GitHub:
https://learngitbranching.js.org/

Networking Basics:
https://explore.skillbuilder.aws/learn/course/11558/aws-networking-fundamentals

Cloud Models:
https://cloud.google.com/training/cloud-digital-leader

What Won’t Work

Watching tutorials without typing commands.
You learn these concepts by breaking and fixing them yourself.


